  "id": "linear-layer-forward",
  "title": "Linear Layer Forward",
  "description": "A linear (fully connected) layer is the most fundamental building block in neural networks. It transforms an input by multiplying with a weight matrix and adding a bias vector. This operation is also called a dense layer or an affine transformation.\n\nGiven an input matrix X (n samples, d_in features), a weight matrix W (d_in x d_out), and a bias vector b (d_out), compute the linear layer output.\n\n### Algorithm\n\n1. For each sample i and output neuron j, compute the weighted sum plus bias:\n\n$$\nY_{ij} = \\sum_{k} X_{ik} \\cdot W_{kj} + b_j\n$$\n\n2. In matrix form:\n\n$$\nY = X \\cdot W + b\n$$\n\nWhere b is broadcast (added to every row of XW).\n\nReturn an n by d_out list containing XW plus the broadcast bias.",
  "seoDescription": "Implement a dense linear layer forward pass by multiplying inputs by weights and adding a bias vector.",
